WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:00.850
John: Good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday.

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:04.310
Wait, what is this background? Am I on a green screen? Am I in Montana?

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:05.630
Hank: Yes, you are.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.010
John: It’s Hank! It's a reunion video! It's happening!

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:12.750
Hank is making his triumphant but temporary
return to vlogbrothers. Hello.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.800
Hank: Hello! I might make another video this week about VidCon.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.540
John: You’re so bad at paternity leave.

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:19.210
Okay, Hank, I got some Question Tuesday questions
from nerdfighters for you.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:20.810
First, how is Orin doing?

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:22.430
Orin is your son.
Hank: He's good!

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:23.770
He's good. He’s a good baby.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.700
John: So cute!

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:26.440
Hank: He’s very cute.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.920
John: It’s almost unbearable.
Hank: I think he may have smiled at me this morning.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:30.760
John: Really?

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:31.440
Hank: Maybe.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.520
He might have just been pooping.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.940
John: Hank, why is there no sequel to The
Fault in Our Stars?

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.620
Hank: It would have been, I think, maybe not
the happiest book.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.780
John: I also don’t really know how it could’ve
happened, but believe me, people in Hollywood

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.300
did make suggestions.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.060
Favorite Disney movie, go!

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.530
Hank: Is “Go” a Disney movie?

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:51.840
John: I thought that that was way too dark
to be a Disney movie.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:57.260
I think it was rated R. I liked the new one
that Lin Manuel Miranda wrote the songs for.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.580
Hank: You know Lin Manuel Miranda wrote a
song for the new Star Wars movie?

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:05.700
*sings*

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:10.580
John: Unfortunately, we don’t have the ability
to clear the rights to that song, but on the

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:15.900
upside, that was not a good enough version
Hank: Yeah! Nobody knows what I was singing.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.529
John: for copyright to come into play.

00:01:17.529 --> 00:01:19.640
What is the most surprising—
Hank: Frozen!

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.840
John: That’s wasn’t the question.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.980
What is the most surprising thing about having
a baby?

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:25.220
Hank: The noise or the poops.

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.560
John: Yes.
Hank: Like, literally surprising
John: Sonic

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:28.780
Hank: like I’ll be like, “Huaahh!!”

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:33.140
Within the first day of Orin being home
John: Yeah.
Hank: he—he pooped with his diaper off

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:34.500
while I was changing it.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.900
John: Oh Hank, that’s a rookie error.

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:36.901
Hank: I’m a rookie.

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:37.661
John: I know.

00:01:37.661 --> 00:01:39.300
Henry pooped on me so many times.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:43.280
Alice pooped on me never, because I would
go in with like seven diapers.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.460
I’d be wearing like a diaper suit of armor.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.680
Hank: I went ahead and tried to catch it with
my hand.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:48.460
John: Nope.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:49.660
Hank: I was like, “Euugh!!”

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:50.520
John: Switch glasses.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.960
Hank: Every time we do this, I’m like, yours
are dirty.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.080
John: Yeah, that’s how I like to see the world:
through smudged lenses.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:59.400
Hank: This eye is pretty much exactly the
same.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.420
John: Oh yeah. Wow.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.540
The left eye is the exact sa—it’s almost
like we’re brothers.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.460
If you could take one book to a desert island,
what book would it be?

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:11.220
I’ve been thinking a lot about this question.
Hank: And just like leave it there so no one
could ever read it again?

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:12.880
John: No!
Hank: Ayn Rand’s The Fountainhead.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:18.580
John: Here is my idea: It’s a book where
if you read it forwards, all the—it’s

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:20.520
just the collected works of Shakespeare.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:26.220
So it’s rich, it’s complicated, it’s
beautiful, and then if you read it backwards,

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.620
like the back sides of the pages
Hank: Okay.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.700
John: are a survival guide for how to live
on a desert island.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:36.000
Hank: I was gonna go with The Kingkiller
trilogy by Patrick Rothfuss, even though the

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.140
last book isn’t out yet, ‘cause I—if
I was gonna get stuck on a desert island,

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.400
I better have that third book.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.260
John: I was gonna say, how terrible would
it be?

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:47.000
You know what would happen, though, because
Pat Rothfuss is such a great guy, you wouldn’t

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:52.260
get to leave the desert island, but an airplane
would fly over, drop the third book when it comes out
Hank: Yeah.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.320
John: and just wave goodbye to you.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:54.380
Hank: Yeah, like a bottle of water.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:56.860
John: And you’d be like, “That’s all
I needed, thanks!”

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.790
Hank, do you have any self-care advice?

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:02.700
Hank: I have lots, but self-care bunny has
better self-care advice than I do.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.450
John: Yeah, self-care bunny is just here to
remind you to be nice to yourself.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.330
Yeah, what did we learn from Nathan Zed’s
video?

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.640
You are a good burrito.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:10.620
Hank: Not the best burrito.

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:14.330
John: You don’t have to be the best, okay,
stop putting so much pressure on yourself.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:15.700
You’re a really good burrito.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.170
Hank: There’s no best burrito.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.170
John: That’s right.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.070
There’s only different kinds of good burritos.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.140
That’s true, actually.
Hank: Yeah.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.360
John: That’s true on many levels.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:26.480
Alright Hank, write an autobiography in five
words.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:33.450
I guess mine would probably be, “Is this
mole a concern?”

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:35.470
I wrote, “He made stuff with John.”

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:38.380
John: Oh God, that’s so nice!

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.120
Hank, thanks for taking time away from your
baby to make a Question Tuesday video.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.180
Hank: Thank Katherine.

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:45.160
John: I will see you right now.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.280
Bye.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.220
Why are—what—when did this become a thing? What? What?

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.640
Do you know Alice does that?

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:51.180
Hank: Thumbs up?

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.120
John: Yeah, whenever you’re like, “Hey,
Alice smile!”

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.720
She doesn’t smile, but she’s like…

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:58.420
Hank: That’s great!

